From: chatgptyukkuri <chatgptyukkuri@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:24:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] zink: don't use conditional rendering buffer usage
 without the extension

VK_BUFFER_USAGE_CONDITIONAL_RENDERING_BIT_EXT is only valid when
VK_EXT_conditional_rendering is enabled. Drivers without the extension,
such as the ARM proprietary driver, may reject the buffer creation, which
breaks query buffer objects.

The conditional rendering paths already check for the extension, so only
add the usage bit when it is available.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LkAyMz3ChWUcwV1bWoNa1Z
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
index dbb23b2..dd086d8 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -549,7 +549,7 @@ create_bci(struct zink_screen *screen, const struct pipe_resource *templ, unsign
 
    bci.usage |= VK_BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE_TEXEL_BUFFER_BIT;
 
-   if (bind & PIPE_BIND_QUERY_BUFFER)
+   if (bind & PIPE_BIND_QUERY_BUFFER && screen->info.have_EXT_conditional_rendering)
       bci.usage |= VK_BUFFER_USAGE_CONDITIONAL_RENDERING_BIT_EXT;
 
    if (templ->flags & PIPE_RESOURCE_FLAG_SPARSE)
